# Pelican source-link syntax ({filename}/{static}); resolves at build time and
# the internal link graph has its own per-PR guard (check_link_graph.py).
%7B(filename|static)%7D
\{(filename|static)\}
# Placeholders and local addresses from code examples - never real links.
^https?://localhost
^https?://host(:|$|/)
^https?://127\.0\.0\.1
# Hosts that block automated checkers while working fine in browsers
# (LinkedIn returns 999 to bots; X/Twitter gates aggressively; hrw.org and
# web.archive.org rate-limit or gate scripted fetches).
^https?://(www\.)?linkedin\.com
^https?://(www\.)?x\.com
^https?://(www\.)?twitter\.com
web\.archive\.org
hrw\.org
# The IAM Blast Radius tool page is a vendored SPA shipped as static files;
# its internal anchors are not crawlable HTML (deploy also --exclude-path's
# output/tools for the same reason).
rivassec\.com/tools/iam-blast-radius
